<title>BELGIUM: EU ministers to vote on beef and pork controls.</title>
<headline>EU ministers to vote on beef and pork controls.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1997-03-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>Farm ministers will be asked to vote on a proposal to simplify health controls on cattle and pigs traded across internal borders next week, a spokesman for the European Union's Dutch presidency told a news briefing on Thursday.</p>
<p>The proposal guaranteeing that member states respect rules on inspection and disease surveillance by imposing penalties on those responsible for outbreaks of disease is opposed by some member states.</p>
<p>&quot;A decision is expected although Germany, Greece and Sweden oppose the proposal and the United Kingdom has a reserve imposed by its own parliamentary procedure,&quot; a Council official said after the briefing. -- Brussels Newsroom +32 2 287 6800</p>
</text>
